PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority (Colleagues 1,2,3,4,5,6,9,10,11,15) select A; minority (7,8,12,14) select E. Core tests from NI 45-106 s.1.1/2.3 (Jan 2021 Ontario): individuals via income (>200k/300k joint, 2 prior yrs + expectation), net fin assets (>1M), or net assets (>=5M); entities via (a) most recent FS showing net assets >=5M or (b) every owner of interests is itself AI. 

A: 3 LPs each qualify individually (Liam/Ace fin-assets; Jack net-assets). GP corp received 6M gifts but no FS/net-asset figure and no proof its owners are AIs → both entity routes fail. B: joint income test met. C: joint net-assets (=5M) met. D: entity net-assets (~10M) met. E: entity net-assets (~5.2M) appears met on facts even if owners fail; debate on whether “FS” requirement or GIC/liability netting blocks it. 

Key unresolved: exact wording on “financial statements” vs. supplied facts, and whether GP gifting implies ownership for all-owners test. Current lean: A fails most cleanly; E qualifies under entity net-assets prong. Will track any new statutory language or clarifications.}

